  "rulesJokerBody": "Two jokers are shuffled into the deck. A joker in hand can be used two ways. Wild: place it on an empty slot of yours as any rank and suit you choose — it counts as one of the round's three placements, goes down face-down, and can be veiled. Strike: point it at any card already on the opponent's board (face-up or hidden). This is a separate action, not one of the three placements; the target's position is visible to them right away. At the reveal, the three cards flip first, then the strike lands: their card is destroyed and the card you chose takes its place, face-up. Until the reveal you can take the joker back by tapping the marked card.",
